{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebSpectrum","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebSpectrum","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.LocalQZetaFunction","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Defs"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.reebSpectrumExample","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.reebSpectrumExample","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebSpectrum.lean#L83-L89","doc":"A witness that `ReebSpectrum` is inhabited. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.HasReebSpectralCoords.coords","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.HasReebSpectralCoords.coords","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebSpectrum.lean#L74-L74","doc":"`αᵢ = q^{ρᵢ}` with `ρᵢ` the `i`-th Reeb eigenvalue. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.HasReebSpectralCoords.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.HasReebSpectralCoords.mk","kind":"ctor","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebSpectrum.lean#L71-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.HasReebSpectralCoords","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.HasReebSpectralCoords","kind":"class","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebSpectrum.lean#L64-L74","doc":"**The identification, as a named hypothesis.** The Frobenius eigenvalues of\n`Z` are the `q`-powers of the Reeb spectrum of `R`.\n\nThis is the open content of bean `qou-qspc`. **No instance is provided** —\nsupplying one would assert the identification, which is exactly what is not\nestablished. Downstream results take it as an explicit `[…]` hypothesis\n(§3b-cond) so the dependency is visible in the type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebSpectrum.is_eigen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebSpectrum.is_eigen","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebSpectrum.lean#L62-L62","doc":"The eigenvalue equation. This is what makes the structure content-bearing:\nan instance must exhibit an operator and vectors satisfying it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebSpectrum.mode_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebSpectrum.mode_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebSpectrum.lean#L59-L59","doc":"A mode is a genuine eigenvector, not the zero vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebSpectrum.spec","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebSpectrum.spec","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebSpectrum.lean#L57-L57","doc":"Their eigenvalues, complex — the critical line is a line in `ℂ`, so a real\nspectrum could not carry the claim `Re(ρ) = 1/2` non-trivially. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebSpectrum.mode","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebSpectrum.mode","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebSpectrum.lean#L54-L54","doc":"The eight fundamental modes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebSpectrum.op","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebSpectrum.op","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebSpectrum.lean#L52-L52","doc":"The operator whose spectrum this is (the Reeb derivation, when\ninstantiated at it). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebSpectrum.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebSpectrum.mk","kind":"ctor","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebSpectrum.lean#L49-L49","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebSpectrum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ReebSpectrum","kind":"structure","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/ReebSpectrum.lean#L44-L62","doc":"**The shape of a Reeb spectrum.** An operator on a `ℂ`-module together with\neight nonzero eigenvectors and their complex eigenvalues.\n\n`H` and `op` are parameters, not claims: this says what it means to *be* a\nspectrum of eight modes, not which operator the framework's `ξ_q` is. ","signatureChunk":0}]}